IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lta-types`
IMPORT `lta-repair`
IMPORT `lta-service-charges`
IMPORT `lta-information`

-- Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this residential lease: do the repairing and fitness covenants
--    apply, and from when; how much of a service charge demand is payable,
--    and may it be withheld; and by when must the landlord's identity or a
--    notice of assignment be given?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Lease case` HAS
    `the lease`                                         IS A `Lease`
    `a service charge demand`                           IS A MAYBE `Service charge demand`
    `the landlord information facts`                    IS A `Landlord information facts`

DECLARE `Lease position` HAS
    `repairing covenant implied (s 11)`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `fitness covenant implied (s 9A)`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `first day the fitness covenant bites`              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `service charge payable`                            IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `service charge may be withheld`                    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `last day to disclose the landlord's identity`      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day for notice of the assignment`             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `end of the old landlord's liability`               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day to request inspection of accounts`        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `latest start of the inspection facilities`         IS A MAYBE DATE

GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO DATE, d IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`apply` f `to the date` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x  THEN JUST (f x)

@ref ss 1, 3, 9A, 9B, 11, 13, 14, 19, 20, 20B, 21B, 22
@export default The position under the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK) for a residential lease: whether the s 11 repairing covenant and the s 9A fitness covenant (England) are implied, and the first day the fitness covenant bites; if a service charge was demanded, the amount payable after ss 19, 20 and 20B and whether it may be withheld under s 21B; the last day to disclose the landlord's identity after a request (s 1), the last day for a new landlord's notice of assignment (s 3(1)), the end of the old landlord's continuing liability (s 3(3A)-(3B)), and the window for inspecting supporting accounts (s 22). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Lease case`  @desc The lease, any service charge demand, and the dates of requests, assignment and notices
GIVETH A `Lease position`
`the lease position for` c MEANS
    `Lease position` WITH
        `repairing covenant implied (s 11)`             IS `section 11 applies to` l
        `fitness covenant implied (s 9A)`               IS `section 9A applies to` l
        `first day the fitness covenant bites`          IS `the first day the fitness covenant bites for` l
        `service charge payable`                        IS
            CONSIDER c's `a service charge demand`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (`the service charge payable on` d)
        `service charge may be withheld`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `a service charge demand`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (`the tenant may withhold payment of` d)
        `last day to disclose the landlord's identity`  IS
            `apply` (GIVEN x YIELD `the last day to disclose the landlord's identity after a request received on` x) `to the date` (f's `identity request received on`)
        `last day for notice of the assignment`         IS
            `apply` (GIVEN x YIELD `the last day for notice of an assignment on` x `with next rent day` (f's `next rent day after the assignment`)) `to the date` (f's `assigned on`)
        `end of the old landlord's liability`           IS `the end of the old landlord's liability under` f
        `last day to request inspection of accounts`    IS
            `apply` (GIVEN x YIELD `the last day to request inspection after a summary obtained on` x) `to the date` (f's `summary obtained on`)
        `latest start of the inspection facilities`     IS
            `apply` (GIVEN x YIELD `the latest start of the inspection facilities after a request on` x) `to the date` (f's `inspection requested on`)
    WHERE
        l MEANS c's `the lease`
        f MEANS c's `the landlord information facts`
